# Curvine-curated FS-semantics syscall suite (derived from upstream 'syscalls').
# Selection: filesystem-related syscall families only (open/read/write/truncate/
# link/rename/mkdir/stat/chmod/chown/utime*/xattr/mmap+sync/getdents/
# inotify/io_uring/mount/handles/path_resolution, ...). Non-FS syscalls
# (signals, sched, ipc, ptrace, network, ...) are out of scope for a
# filesystem CI gate.
# Additionally dropped: every tag that FAILED (TCONF/timeout/suspect) in the
# 2026-08-26 Curvine full-syscalls baseline on rocky9 kernel 6.17:
#  - TCONF env-skips (16-bit chown variants, CAP_*, loop devices, ...)
#  - timeout-slow fd/lock floods (each close = FUSE RELEASE RPC)
#  - kernel-version-dependent suspects
# Post-validation drops (2026-08-27 full syscalls-cv run on Curvine FUSE):
#  - mmap16: tst_checkpoint 10s race (kernel mmap-race regression test),
#    flaky under FUSE timing; not an FS-semantics check
#  - readahead02: all 11 semantic assertions pass, but the page-cache
#    accounting warning forces a nonzero exit on FUSE (consistent)
# Runner note: sync-family tests (fsync01/04, syncfs01, sync_file_range02)
